    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A first name, Muslim or Christian, and a family name from the father that usually tells people his community: Kamara, Sesay, Bangura and Kanu are Temne; Kallon, Lahai and Bockarie are Mende; Cole, Macauley and Davies are Krio, from the families of freed people who settled Freetown. Temne and Mende families are mostly Muslim, and the Krio mostly Christian, and many families are both. Kono first-borns are often Sahr (boy) or Finda (girl), and people are often called by a nickname or 'Pa' or 'Mammy' with their first name.",
